            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen Kearns"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My grandmother &amp; my mother always used a version of this recipe, and now, so do I. Our only modifications were/are to use either whole milk or half &amp; half in place of the evaporated milk and water, AND to pre-cook the oysters in their own liquid and at least a half of a stick of real butter, just until the edges curl, and after all ingredients have melded together, to put into the refrigerator to age until the next day.",
